[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]keymap-log-level[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: keymap-log-level' section: restore the `sase` logger level in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the TUI log-setup fixture and scope the keymap registry test's caplog to[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the emitting logger.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Attribute residual-freeze soak failures to the fixed paths, [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]not the wall-clock window[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]soak-attribution[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: soak-attribution' section: make the lowered-threshold soak [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]assertion fail only on watchdog events implicating the deliberately [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocked paths, so unrelated bounded renders on loaded runners stop [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failing it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove the host `$HOME` dependency from the axe editor visual [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]snapshots[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]visual-home-path[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: visual-home-path' section: derive the axe writable-scope fixture[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path from the real home directory so the tilde abbreviation renders [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identically on every host, then regenerate the seven affected goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate the neighbor-badge and prompt-caret snapshots on rendered[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]output[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]visual-capture-races[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: visual-capture-races' section: reproduce and fix the two CI-only[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PNG capture races by waiting on the painted frame instead of internal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]footer layout inputs and widget focus state.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix spurious SQLITE_BUSY in the sase-core telemetry store[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-sqlite-busy[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: core-sqlite-busy' section: in the sase-core repo, make write [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]transactions use BEGIN IMMEDIATE and make the WAL journal-mode pragma [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contention-tolerant so concurrent telemetry writers stop failing with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`database is locked`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Align sase's `sase-core-rs` window with a published core [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]release[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-release-window[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-sqlite-busy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase: core-release-window' section: land a sase-core release that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contains the 20 bindings sase requires, then point sase's pyproject [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]window at that published version and stop the speculative minor ratchet.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-93","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-93.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-488a2c0dfa79436bfb39c492c862c739","started_at":"2026-07-25T11:28:09.348132+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"5b9581fb7dd226d4aa47ffbf41bc781bcf5d38301a267618b2c10e3ccf3ce07c","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-93.land/chat.md","size_bytes":2413},"commits":{"digest":"b2a0b4ef8c75de33976a548bac008cf20c67de9597beaa932ba0a118af71dddf","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sas